{"step_index":64,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-12T04:50:59Z","content":"I have fully built and verified **AegisOS**, a complete hackathon-winning solution engineered directly for the **\"Rescue AI from the chat window\"** track.\n\nDetailed technical documentation and verification logs are recorded in [walkthrough.md](file:///C:/Users/Piyush/.gemini/antigravity/brain/e426a91e-3961-4012-84ca-1849c4385ef7/walkthrough.md).\n\n---\n\n### 🌟 How AegisOS Conquers the Hackathon Prompt\n\n| Challenge Requirement | How AegisOS Delivers |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **\"Rescue AI from the chat window\"** | **Zero Chat UI**: Operates via a cyberpunk ambient **Mission Control HUD** docked on the screen. No prompt boxes, no conversational fluff. |\n| **\"Give it hands\"** | **OS-Level Motor Control** ([`actuator.py`](file:///C:/Users/Piyush/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/aegis_os/aegis/actuator.py)): Smooth cursor kinematics, accessibility targeting, and keyboard typing directly into legacy enterprise software and web apps. |\n| **\"Memory\" (Self-Learning & Adaptation)** | **Episodic State Graph** ([`memory.py`](file:///C:/Users/Piyush/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/aegis_os/aegis/memory.py)): Caches spatial UI anchors into \"muscle memory\". If an app moves a button (UI drift), it relocalizes the element, updates the graph, and self-heals without human intervention. |\n| **\"Sense of Boundaries\" (Guardrails & Trust)** | **Deterministic Boundary Hypervisor** ([`hypervisor.py`](file:///C:/Users/Piyush/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/aegis_os/aegis/hypervisor.py)): Pre-flight mathematical boundary checking (e.g. $\\$5,000$ ceiling, prohibited actions), atomic state snapshotting, automatic rollback, and cryptographic Proof-of-Boundary. |\n\n---\n\n### 🚀 Running the Live 3-Act Demo\n\nYou can run the live demonstration right now on your screen:\n\n```powershell\ncd C:\\Users\\Piyush\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\aegis_os\npython run_demo.py\n```\n\nClick **`[▶ START LIVE 3-ACT DEMO]`** on the HUD to watch:\n1. **Act I (The Hands)**: The agent takes the mouse, glides across the screen, fills out a payment voucher, and clicks process.\n2. **Act II (Self-Learning)**: The target ERP triggers \"Chaos Mode\" (the button shifts $\\sim 240\\text{px}$ across the screen). AegisOS detects the drift, self-heals, updates its episodic memory, and hits the new target.\n3. **Act III (Boundaries & Trust)**: An unauthorized $\\$48,900$ invoice attempting to purge audit logs arrives. The hypervisor intercepts the action **before the mouse even moves**, halts actuation, and renders cryptographic Proof-of-Boundary.\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Recommend opening **`C:\\Users\\Piyush\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\aegis_os`** as your active workspace in your IDE. You can read the complete 3-minute presentation script in [`README.md`](file:///C:/Users/Piyush/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/aegis_os/README.md)."}
